1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,200
Hello and welcome.

2
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:02,240
This is Mala.

3
00:00:02,606 --> 00:00:08,804
I'm excited to have you join me on this hands-on journey into the world of AI agents and agentic AI.

4
00:00:09,486 --> 00:00:19,760
Whether you are a beginner looking to understand AI agents from the ground up or a developer who wants to build real-world AI applications using today's leading frameworks,

5
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:25,188
this course is designed to take you from the fundamentals to advanced production ready systems.

6
00:00:25,614 --> 00:00:32,560
By the end of this course, you'll understand not only how AI agents work, but also how to design, build and

7
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:38,660
evaluate intelligent autonomous systems using the most popular AI agent frameworks available today.

8
00:00:39,246 --> 00:00:41,156
Let's take a quick tour of everything you'll learn.

9
00:00:41,806 --> 00:00:44,292
We begin by setting up your development environment.

10
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:53,680
I'll show you how to install Anaconda, work with Jupyter Notebook, use Markdown for documentation, configure Visual Studio Code, and Google Colab

11
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,612
so you're ready to build projects throughout the course.

12
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,460
Next, we'll cover Python fundamentals.

13
00:00:59,918 --> 00:01:08,164
Even if you are new to Python or need a quick refresher, we'll review variables, data types, packages, control flow,

14
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:17,760
loops, functions, and the most important Python data structures, including lists, tuples, strings, sets, and dictionaries.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,320
This gives everyone a solid programming foundation before we move into AI development.

16
00:01:22,670 --> 00:01:27,600
Once the environment and Python basics are ready, we'll begin exploring AI agents.

17
00:01:27,886 --> 00:01:38,180
You'll learn what AI agents really are, why they've become one of the hottest topics in artificial intelligence and how to separate the real capabilities from the hype.

18
00:01:39,086 --> 00:01:48,080
We'll dive deep into agent architecture and explore different levels of autonomy, helping you understand what makes an AI system truly agentic.

19
00:01:48,782 --> 00:01:57,092
After that, we'll explore the technology that powers modern AI agents, large language models, or LLMs.

20
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:06,564
You'll learn what LLMs are, why they're called large, how they evolved over time, why model parameters matter,

21
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:13,060
and how these models are trained from massive data sets into intelligent reasoning systems.

22
00:02:13,582 --> 00:02:18,948
With that foundation in place, we'll start building AI agents using Langchain.

23
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:27,680
You'll create your first AI agent, understand how tool calling enables agents to interact with external systems, learn the React

24
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:33,732
reasoning framework, and build intelligent agents that can reason, plan and act step by step.

25
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:41,252
Before diving deeper into specific tools, we'll take a guided tour of today's AI agent ecosystem.

26
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:46,720
You'll compare popular frameworks including Langchain, Langgraph,

27
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:55,492
Crew AI, AutoGen, Lama Index Langflow, Agno, N8N, and other emerging platforms.

28
00:02:56,302 --> 00:03:02,724
We will discuss code first, low code and no-code approaches so you can understand where each framework fits and when to use it.

29
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:08,080
Next, we will move into Langflow where you will build AI agents visually.

30
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:17,380
You'll learn how to install Langflow, solve common setup issues, and create practical applications including a URL reading agent,

31
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:23,556
a mathematical reasoning agent, a multi-agent travel planner, and a YouTube analysis agent.

32
00:03:24,206 --> 00:03:28,560
From there, we'll explore hugging face small agents.

33
00:03:29,006 --> 00:03:38,800
You'll understand the difference between tool calling agents and code agents before building research agents, vision agents, and multi-agents AI systems.

34
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:45,796
We'll also introduce Lang Fuse so you can observe, trace and evaluate your AI agents like production systems.

35
00:03:46,318 --> 00:03:51,140
Then we'll move into one of the most important concepts in modern AI applications.

36
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:54,480
Retrieval augmented generation or RAG.

37
00:03:54,880 --> 00:04:06,596
Using Lama Index, you will build your first RAG application, learn how agentic RAG extends traditional retrieval systems, and develop an intelligent AI assistant that combines retrieval

38
00:04:06,958 --> 00:04:09,600
reasoning and external knowledge sources.

39
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:17,092
After that, we'll master Langgraph, one of the most powerful frameworks for creating production-ready AI workflows.

40
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:26,148
You'll build an AI-powered email automation workflow, a vision assistant, a vision assistant with email integration using SendGrid,

41
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:31,850
and an AI resume optimization agent using Langgraph, Langchain, and Pydantic.

42
00:04:32,654 --> 00:04:38,532
Finally, we'll dive into Crew AI and learn how to build collaborative multi-agent systems.

43
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:50,000
You'll create a multi agent, content creation framework, build an AI powered sales outreach system, automate, resume and interview preparation with an AI job application system,

44
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:59,204
and finish the course by developing a complete multi agent AI stock trading system that brings together many of the concepts you've learned throughout the course.

45
00:05:00,110 --> 00:05:07,952
Throughout this course, you will gain a practical experience with Langchain Langraph, Cru AI, Lama Index Langflow,

46
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:16,272
Hugging Face Molagens, Langfuse, React, tool calling agentic rank, multi-agent

47
00:05:16,512 --> 00:05:19,492
systems, and production ready AI workflows.

48
00:05:20,014 --> 00:05:22,192
This course is designed to be highly practical.

49
00:05:22,352 --> 00:05:31,392
Rather than focusing only on theory, we'll build real world projects together so you can understand how modern AI agent systems are designed and implemented.

50
00:05:31,632 --> 00:05:34,272
I encourage you to experiment with the examples.

