4106
06:02:59,120 --> 06:03:05,828
So multi-agent structures allow us to separate memories between different subtasks with great benefits.

4107
06:03:06,160 --> 06:03:08,676
The first one is divide and conquer.

4108
06:03:08,960 --> 06:03:11,812
That is, each agent is more focused on its core task.

4109
06:03:12,110 --> 06:03:13,840
So the agent can perform better.

4110
06:03:14,080 --> 06:03:22,692
That is, each agent focuses on a specific task or single responsibility that simplifies complex problems by breaking them into parts.

4111
06:03:22,880 --> 06:03:25,412
And the next one is parallelism and speed.

4112
06:03:25,680 --> 06:03:32,964
Agents can work either sequentially or in parallel with less overhead so they can complete tasks faster.

4113
06:03:33,294 --> 06:03:35,280
And improved focus and memory.

4114
06:03:35,470 --> 06:03:41,444
Separating memories reduces the count of input tokens at each step, which will reduce latency and cost.

4115
06:03:41,774 --> 06:03:46,160
Because if one agent is performing all the tasks, then it consumes more memory, right?

4116
06:03:46,350 --> 06:03:52,548
And whatever the response we get from one thought, action, observation loop will be appended to the agent memory.

4117
06:03:52,800 --> 06:03:57,200
And if we have more loops, it consumes more tokens to complete the task, right?

4118
06:03:57,390 --> 06:04:01,680
