5555
07:53:47,118 --> 07:53:48,580
These are the five workflows

5556
07:53:49,294 --> 07:53:54,020
sequential, hierarchical, hybrid, parallel, and async.

5557
07:53:54,670 --> 07:54:01,860
Sequential flow means the first agent completes its task and then it will hand it over to the second agent and so on.

5558
07:54:02,510 --> 07:54:04,292
Next one is hierarchical flow.

5559
07:54:04,814 --> 07:54:07,780
There will be a manager agent which will manage the agents.

5560
07:54:08,334 --> 07:54:14,532
The task will be received by the manager agent, and the manager agent will decide whom to assign the task to.

5561
07:54:15,342 --> 07:54:19,108
So here there is no sequence unlike sequential agent workflow.

5562
07:54:19,406 --> 07:54:20,644
The next one is hybrid.

5563
07:54:21,198 --> 07:54:23,716
This is the combination of sequential and hierarchical.

5564
07:54:24,078 --> 07:54:25,860
The other one is parallel.

5565
07:54:26,446 --> 07:54:30,788
This is used when we want multiple agents working in parallel at the same time.

5566
07:54:31,406 --> 07:54:39,360
Let's say we have to sift through some 5000 documents, then we can spin up five agents, assign 1000 documents to each.

5567
07:54:39,694 --> 07:54:42,148
Once the work is done, then we can merge the output.

5568
07:54:42,638 --> 07:54:44,246
And the last one is async.

5569
07:54:45,040 --> 07:54:48,640
Here, each task is executed independently by each agent.

5570
07:54:49,102 --> 07:54:51,120
