5572
07:54:52,400 --> 07:54:56,452
Let's also understand the differences among all these workflows.

5573
07:54:57,198 --> 07:55:01,188
Think of these as different ways a team of AI agents can work together.

5574
07:55:01,774 --> 07:55:05,760
In a sequential flow, agents work one after another.

5575
07:55:06,158 --> 07:55:11,364
The first agent completes its task, then passes the result to the next agent, and so on.

5576
07:55:11,822 --> 07:55:17,860
For example, agent A writes an article and once it's finished, agent B edits it.

5577
07:55:18,286 --> 07:55:26,148
In a hierarchical flow, there is a manager or leader agent that assigns tasks to other agents and coordinates their work.

5578
07:55:26,720 --> 07:55:33,508
For example, a manager agent asks one agent to do research and another agent to write a report.

5579
07:55:34,702 --> 07:55:38,660
And a hybrid flow combines both hierarchical and sequential approaches.

5580
07:55:39,150 --> 07:55:45,028
A leader agent delegates work to multiple agents and their outputs are later combined or reviewed in sequence.

5581
07:55:45,440 --> 07:55:52,324
For example, a leader assigns research to two agents and then a reviewer agent combines and checks their results.

5582
07:55:52,974 --> 07:55:57,476
In a parallel flow, multiple agents work at the same time on different tasks.

5583
07:55:57,902 --> 07:56:00,932
They do not need to wait for each other to finish before starting.

5584
07:56:01,440 --> 07:56:06,756
For example, two agents independently research different topics simultaneously.

5585
07:56:06,960 --> 07:56:14,960
In an async flow, agents work independently and do not wait for other tasks to complete before continuing.

5586
07:56:15,406 --> 07:56:18,116
Tasks can start, run and finish whenever they are ready.

5587
07:56:18,400 --> 07:56:24,880
For example, an agent sends periodic status updates while other agents are still working on their tasks.

5588
07:56:25,166 --> 07:56:26,720
Here is a simple analogy.

5589
07:56:27,214 --> 07:56:30,180
For example, consider a school project.

5590
07:56:30,830 --> 07:56:35,684
Sequential flow could be student A writes the report and then student B reviews it.

5591
07:56:36,046 --> 07:56:40,640
In hierarchical flow, the team leader assigns tasks to all students.

5592
07:56:40,942 --> 07:56:46,532
In hybrid flow, team leader assigns tasks, then another student combines everyone's work.

5593
07:56:47,022 --> 07:56:51,972
Parallel flow could be all students work on different sections at the same time.

5594
07:56:52,462 --> 07:56:58,756
And finally, async flow, students submit their parts whenever they finish without waiting for others.

